  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Mozambique and the United Nations (UN) in Mozambique signed the United Nations Sustainable Development Partnership Framework 2022-2026. An essential preliminary step in developing the Cooperation Framework was the Common Country Analysis (CCA), the UN independent, impartial and collective assessment of a country&#x2019;s situation in relation to the achievement of the SDGs. The CCA has taken into account the application of International Labour Standards to enhance the possibility of the issue being addressed in the Cooperation Framework. The CCA has identified decent work priorities that are well informed and anchored in the use and application of international labour standards with a view to their inclusion in CCAs and Cooperation Frameworks. The ILO being a member of the United Nations Country Team (UNCT) and Results Groups participated in various meetings discussing the development of the draft CCA for UN Mozambique. The ILO input into the CCA has since been incorporated into the final document. The ILOStat database has been used as the basis for providing Labour market landscape for the CCA.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2.2. Percentage of new UN Cooperation Frameworks that include measures to address issues raised by the ILO supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Maritime Labour Convention, 2006, as amended (MLC, 2006) was ratified and registered with the ILO on 25 May 2021. The ILO provided technical assistance to the Government in order to assist them with the finalization of the process of ratification of the MLC, in particular concerning the declaration on social security and the amendments to the MLC, 2006.   In 2020- 2021, the ILO maritime team held several meetings with the Mozambique delegates in Geneva and followed up with messages by mail and in-country contacts with the Ministry of Labour. In 2021, a gap analysis was conducted and tripartite constituents were trained on the MLC, 2006 in order to assist the Mozambique Government with the implementation of the Convention.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.2. Number of ratifications of up-to-date technical Conventions, including those recommended by the Governing Body in the context of the Standards Review Mechanism</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
